title HUNK49 — the touchable Photos editor: a gesture edits, the view repaints, from one cursor
prompt Continue the autonomous loop — next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop only at custody gates.
think HUNK48 gave the Photos editing arc its input seam (a gesture becomes one EditCursor move); HUNK13 already down-mapped an edit-list onto Skate. The two halves stood uncoupled — the capstone crux, parallel to HUNK47 for scroll, is one surface that owns both, so a device touches and watches the same image.
think Lindy-first crux-first picked it: read every time a keeper edits, composing only proven parts. Confirmed the cross-assembly composition is already clean — cursor_preview.rye (brushstroke/) binds edit_cursor + edit_preview + image_skate, and edit_cursor/photo_edits are symlinked into brushstroke/; I added brushstroke/edit_input.rye -> ../image/edit_input.rye so the seam resolves there too.
think Shape: EditTouchView { cursor, cols, rows } — open validates the grid against the down-map ceiling (BadView caught once, so paint never refuses on dimension); gesture delegates to edit_input.apply over the owned cursor; paint renders edit_preview.preview of exactly cursor.applied(). The crux: paint is always the picture of the cursor the gesture just moved — it cannot drift, structurally, the same one-graph discipline HUNK47 used for scroll.
obs Caught the recurring apostrophe red the HUNK39/40/42/43 logs each booked: the selftest GREEN line held apostrophes (cursor's, paint's) that break the witness single-quoted shell grep, so the whole printf mangled and the green grep failed though the selftest was GREEN. Fixed by rephrasing the print line apostrophe-free — the same reflex those logs named. A lantern that fires this many times wants a loom (a grep helper that quotes safely); named as a ratchet, not booked this round.
obs Also split two compound asserts at open (assert(a and b)) the TAME ban flagged — one positive invariant per line. Witness reads behavior on glass: a commit tracks the flip (left cell red->blue), undo/redo walk the picture, paint equals a direct preview (no drift), two paints byte-identical, painting never walks the cursor, a bad grid and a committed out-of-bounds crop each refuse by name. HUNK48 seam and HUNK13 preview GREEN beneath; TAME bans clean, width exit 0.
loom witness=hunk_edit_touch_view_witness image=8x8_two_tone grid=2x2 gestures=commit_flip_h,undo,redo drift_check=paint==edit_preview.preview(applied) refusals=BadView,OutOfBounds
file brushstroke/edit_touch_view.rye HUNK49 — EditTouchView binds HUNK48's gesture seam and HUNK13's preview to one cursor; paint shows exactly where the edit history stands.
file brushstroke/edit_input.rye symlink to image/edit_input.rye so the seam resolves in the brushstroke assembly.
file tools/hunk_edit_touch_view_witness.rish proves the surface on metal — a gesture edits, the view tracks, the picture never drifts, a bad grid and a bad crop refuse.
file active-designing/20260813-203500_hunk-edit-touch-view-exploration.md self-approved design read.
file work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md git nib refreshed in this same work commit.
recommend keep-going — the Photos editing interaction now closes symmetrically with the browse interaction (HUNK47). HUNK50 could bind a raw touch (a tap on a gesture strip, a swipe left/right) to gesture as HUNK46 did for scroll, record a gesture stream content-addressed (composing HUNK12's edit store), or open a fresh Season-A / double-seat journey. The served-market module-assembly ruling and hardware buys stay Keaton's gates.
